The lifecycle handling around that `seq` gate is Devboule's own and
diverges from herdr on purpose: herdr removes a source's sequence on a
witnessed process exit and re-anchors under process confirmation
(`herdr-src/src/terminal/state.rs:697-699`), while Devboule observes no
process and instead keys each counter by `(source, agent_session_id)` and
starts a key over when a `startup`/`resume`/`new`/`fork`/`branch`
report's seq does not beat the stored one.

